  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall begin not later than three years from the date of this decision.\r\nReason: In order to comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended by Section 51 of the Planning and Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and specifications: [300_P, 301_P, 6433_001_3, Unnumbered Fire Statement, Unnumbered Cover Letter. Received: 24/09/2025.\r\n101_P, Unnumbered Operations Email. Received: 11/11/2025].\r\nReason: In order to ensure the development is carried out in accordance with the planning permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved plans.\r\nReason: In order to safeguard the appearance of the area.",
    "Condition : 4 - Notwithstanding the submitted details and prior to occupation, full details (including manufacturer's specifications) of all cycle stands for the occupants of, and visitors to, the development shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. \r\nThe approved facilities shall be fully implemented and made available for use before any part of the development is first occupied and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction. \r\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives.",
    "Condition : 5 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details of the Electric Vehicle Charging Points, each capable of  a minimum output of 7.2kW, are submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include manufacturer's specifications and the number of spaces provided with active and passive capabilities shall comply with the London Plan standards.\r\nThe charging points shall be installed in accordance with the approved details, with photographic evidence submitted to the Local Planning Authority upon completion, and so maintained at all times thereafter.\r\nReason: In order to promote sustainable modes of transport.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to first occupation of the development, full details of the [one] blue badge parking bay shown on approved plan [101_P] shall be installed in accordance with the approved details and so maintained at all times thereafter.\r\nReason: In order to ensure that the development complies with inclusive design principles"
  ],
